closed_at: "2026-07-16T17:19:00.621Z"
author: codex-root
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Actionable source/security/documentation findings are fixed or explicitly tracked; Secret history scan and package content inspection pass
definition_of_ready: Repository file inventory and high-risk pattern scan collected.
parent: searx-recovery-plan
reviewer: repository-owner
risk: high
confidence: 80
sprint: 2026-07-recovery
release: next
resolution: "Completed source, packaging, workflow, documentation, and live repository-security audit with immediate remediations and a measured architecture backlog."
expected_result: "Actionable findings are fixed or governed with detailed follow-up, and security/package inspection surfaces are clean."
actual_result: Immediate findings are implemented; secret/security controls are enabled; the remaining large modularization is tracked under searx-modular-command-architecture.
comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T16:58:05.702Z",codex-root,Native GitHub secret scanning is disabled; gitleaks workflow currently provides the repository scan.
  "2026-07-16T17:12:24.645Z",codex-root,Enabled and verified native GitHub secret scanning plus push protection; non-provider and validity-check add-ons are unavailable for this repository tier and remained disabled.
  "2026-07-16T17:12:24.645Z",codex-root,Pinned all workflow actions to current full commit SHAs and enabled repository-level SHA pin enforcement.
  "2026-07-16T17:19:00.118Z",codex-root,"Audit fixed URL trust and bounded-fetch security, Windows browser spawning, hermetic E2E lifecycle, native GitHub security controls, workflow SHA pinning, documentation, and coverage enforcement."
  "2026-07-16T17:19:00.118Z",codex-root,"Future architectural decomposition is tracked as searx-modular-command-architecture with source measurements, sequencing guidance, tests, and acceptance criteria."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T16:58:05.702Z",codex-root,Distinguish immediate fixes from larger roadmap improvements while retaining detailed evidence.
learnings[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-16T16:58:05.702Z",codex-root,Baseline behavior is green so changes should be justified by concrete risk or maintenance evidence.
  "2026-07-16T17:12:24.645Z",codex-root,Repository security controls were materially weaker than the Gitleaks workflow alone suggested; live settings inspection is required.
  "2026-07-16T17:19:00.118Z",codex-root,"Verification should be treated as an audit feedback loop: the first clean-host E2E run exposed a hidden daemon dependency that the unit suite could not reveal."
